events.content:
Now I understand the setup. Gravity UI uikit has a `Toaster` (useToaster hook) for toast notifications. The task: a button in the corner of the screen, click shows a toast that auto-disappears.

Gravity UI approach:
- `ToasterProvider` (or create `new Toaster()`), `useToaster()` hook with `add({name, title, content, autoHidingTimeout})`.

Let me check what's available in @gravity-ui/uikit v7. `ToasterProvider` exists with `useToaster`. The toast config: `{ name, title, content, type?, autoHidingTimeout }`. Default timeout... Toaster has `DEFAULT_TIMEOUT = 5000`. Actually in Gravity UI, Toast props: `autoHidingTimeout?: number | false`. Default is 5000ms I believe.

Implementation plan:

App.tsx:
```tsx
import {Button, ToasterProvider, useToaster} from '@gravity-ui/uikit';
import {Bell} from '@gravity-ui/icons'; // icons may not be installed
```

Check if @gravity-ui/icons is installed — package.json doesn't list it. So avoid icons or use text/emoji.

Structure:

```tsx
import {useCallback} from 'react';
import {Button, ToasterProvider, useToaster} from '@gravity-ui/uikit';

function CornerButton() {
  const {add} = useToaster();

  const showToast = useCallback(() => {
    add({
      name: 'corner-toast-' + Date.now(),
      title: 'Готово!',
      content: 'Это всплывающее уведомление. Оно исчезнет само через несколько секунд.',
      autoHidingTimeout: 4000,
    });
  }, [add]);

  return (
    <Button
      view="action"
      size="l"
      onClick={showToast}
      style={{position: 'fixed', right: 24, bottom: 24, zIndex: 1}}
    >
      Показать уведомление
    </Button>
  );
}

export function App() {
  return (
    <ToasterProvider>
      <div style={{padding: 24}}>
        <h1>...</h1>
        <CornerButton />
      </div>
    </ToasterProvider>
  );
}
```

Note: unique name per toast so multiple clicks show multiple toasts (or same name replaces). Using Date.now gives stacking toasts — nice.

Also StrictMode double-render is fine.

Check ToasterProvider exists in v7.43: yes, `ToasterProvider` was added in @gravity-ui/uikit 6.x. It accepts optional `toaster` prop. `useToaster` returns `{add, remove, update}`.

Toast type in Gravity UI: add({name, title, content, type: 'success' | 'info' | ... , isClosable, autoHidingTimeout, actions}). Default autoHidingTimeout is 5000 (DEFAULT_TIMEOUT in Toaster). Explicitly setting it is good.

Then verify build: npm run build (tsc --noEmit && vite build). Let me write the file and build.

Button corner: "в углу экрана" — bottom-right is typical. Fixed positioning.

Let me also make sure `ToasterProvider` import path: it's exported from '@gravity-ui/uikit' root. Yes.

Write App.tsx, then run npm run build to typecheck.

